# Local overrides. The deployed site does not need this file — the API key
# lives in Netlify's environment, never a repo file. Never put a real key here either: anything that was ever in a
# local .env is rotated (docs/SECURITY.md, docs/OPS.md scenario 10).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The domain. Unset, the app calls itself joinniyyah.com (src/lib/site.ts),
# the address we own, baked into every link it hands out and every share
# card. Set it only to move: if the domain were ever lost, set this to the new
# host (or getniyyah.netlify.app, which keeps serving) and redeploy —
# docs/OPS.md, scenario 8. See docs/OPS.md.
# VITE_SITE_HOST=joinniyyah.com

# Where a person reaches a human: the contact link on Home and Trust. The
# default, salaam@joinniyyah.com, is only real once that domain receives mail —
# until then set this to an address a person reads (docs/OPS.md).
# VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=salaam@joinniyyah.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately NOT listed here. It belongs only in Netlify's
# environment — plaintext to the team on the free plan, which refuses the
# secret scope (docs/OPS.md), so rotation is the control — because it is read by netlify/functions/guide.ts
# on the server and must never reach the browser bundle or the repository.
#
# Setting it switches the live Guide on, which means members' answers start
# leaving their device — so the Trust screen's privacy copy must be rewritten in
# the same change. See the README.
#
# FOUNDER_KEY is not listed here either. It gates every readout — the ladder,
# the couple tally, the backup, the safety queue, the guide's health check —
# behind `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
# Unset means CLOSED: every readout answers 401 until it is set
# (netlify/shared/founder.ts). This file said the opposite until
# 2026-09-23, long after that stopped being true (docs/SECURITY.md, O4).
# Use a long random value (32+ characters), set it in Netlify's environment
# and as a GitHub Actions secret of the same name (the health run reads
# /health with it), and confirm a bare GET on /health returns 401. See
# docs/OPS.md.
